9. Limitations and Open Challenges

· Battery endurance: The operational timeline (§5.4) accounts for hot‑swaps and tethered operation. Battery‑health‑aware task scheduling, inspired by recent work on fleet sizing to prevent synchronised battery depletion, ensures mission completion.
· Metallic‑environment physics: The stainless‑steel hull causes magnetic interference and RF multipath. Mitigation includes spread‑spectrum UWB modulation and magnetic shielding of the CMD’s eddy‑current probe.
· Launch‑pad acoustic/vibration environment: Rocket‑plume‑generated vibro‑acoustic loads during propellant loading are measured using onboard IMU spectra; vibration‑tolerant image stabilisation (optical‑flow + gimbal) maintains sub‑mm hover precision.
· LLM hallucination: The KG + RAG + deterministic‑verifier architecture (§4.2.4) is mandatory.
· Regulatory pathway: BVLOS waivers will be pursued in collaboration with the relevant launch‑site authority; a phased regulatory engagement plan is included in Appendix B.
· Point‑cloud scalability: Multi‑drone LiDAR at sub‑mm resolution over a 120 m vehicle generates petabytes per inspection. Semantic compression and level‑of‑detail management are addressed in WP4.

